rved as a crucial nexus for diverse cultures, including the Romans, Byzantines, and Ottomans, thus embodying the confluence of civilizations. Its significance is underscored by its remarkable architecture, including the impressive city walls, which are among the best-preserved in the world, and its historical role as a center of trade, culture, and governance.

